  "rules": [
    "Translate only the value. Never change a key.",
    "Keep every placeholder exactly as written and in the same form: %lld, %@, %%. You may reorder them to fit grammar.",
    "A key may contain both %lld and %@. %lld is always a count; %@ is always text.",
    "Keep the middle dot separator ' · ' as ' · ' where the key has it.",
    "Do not add or remove trailing periods, question marks, or ellipsis characters. Match the source punctuation exactly.",
    "Use the polite/formal register Apple uses on macOS for the language.",
    "Keep sentences short. These are UI labels and buttons, not prose.",
    "Numbers stay as placeholders. Never write a literal digit where the source has %lld.",
    "For a plural entry, supply all CLDR categories that language uses.",
    "Do not translate an entry into English for a non-English language.",
    "If a key is a bare symbol or technical token with no words (for example '1080p' or 'MB'), copy it unchanged."
  ]
